    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0486" n="382" xml:id="pg382"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1890-03-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 9,
                    1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Blaine</hi>: I have the pleasure to send you
                    herewith the memorandum prepared by Mr. Tupper on the seal fishery question, to
                    which he has appended a note by Mr. Dawson, an eminent Canadian official.</p>
                <p>Believe me, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>






